rom the ford** (he rode a tail-board on the level from the 295th to the 298th and walked the hills and the cut). He has said "Noted" twice (the grade; the knee) — it is Cael's word and he says so. He is on the contract's count as one of "your six"; he has not asked to join the six and nobody has spoken of it. He does not know the mechanism, the eleventh (his own), the twelfth, the two words or the date; he knows that he is not told and that it is "six people's". (5) **The grade:** three marks — a stroke alone (a box ruled and EMPTY; no first-tier site exists on any sheet); a stroke with one bar (the four places; stake thirty-two; the dead surveyor's book); a stroke with two bars (six sheets of a fifth place). "A mark is a grade … what he's *for* … how *old* the thing is" (Karis). **Ages counted from the office's first sheet for each place: the Fallow 61, the Stair 94, the Hall 138, the place behind the iron 206**; the fifth place has two unread signs for its figure ("older than two hundred and six"). **Oldest-last.** The office's run from the fourth place to the fifth is "three days past the iron, a little less"; its compass point and its figure in lengths have not been said aloud. The fourth line of the leaf's list: the mark, over *those who are kindled* and *what is set*, level; *three*. Karis has said none of the list's numbers aloud and five of its nine lines are unturned. **Nothing joins this to lamps, sigils, plates, Arbiters or stations**; "four hundred years" stood once, in Cael's log of the 298th, as his own inference — in this movement it may stand only where this packet's plan fixes it. (6) **Hesk's dividers** have been opened twice, by Karis, on Cael's loan; Cael has never opened them. The hide has a clean sheet pinned to its eastern edge with a prick at the divider's point and the pencil line ruled through it and a hand's breadth past. Stake thirty-two is in the tarred case, never driven. (7) **Oryn** knows the two self-readings, the eleventh and the twelfth; her ruling was "not on my plank". **Her finding** ("There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow* …") is known to Cael and Lira. **Cael's own — the twelfth turned inward unbidden under her hands: *still*, then *set* — is told to NO ONE**, and the next word was not let come; Lira knows only that something unasked came and is waiting; the log holds four reasons and the ruling *hold*. Oryn has not heard the leaf ("Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table."). Cleon's warning has "begun to lean". She walks east in the middle of the file with the mule, on nobody's count: three holds owed on her round; "I'm a stop on my own route." (8) **Bodies at dawn on the 299th:** Brom's left shoulder mended, the right re-tied, both arms to shoulder height; Lira's arm released ("It's an arm."); Karis's stitches out, linen on, "Write. Don't lean."; Teague's right wrist in linen under the leather. (9) **Watchers:** a horseman a mile behind on the 296th and a riderless horse in the western alders on the 297th; nothing seen east of the river; no face, name or base. (10) **Seln's case is "shut"** — never write "unopened" or "locked … unopened" (this packet's cutaway note says so and is overridden here); on his chest; contents unnamed; no count of years printed.
