   864	### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
   865	**Calendar.** The night of the **three hundred and fifth day past the Line**, on a shelf of shale under a step, four or five miles short of a square gap in the hills to the east, a day's walk past the fourth place. Days on the page: 299 (the ridge; the Stair's brow; the beck), 300 (the cairn at noon; the track; the hall's marsh at dusk), 301 (the east road; the dead hold), 302 (the chock-stones; the ridge; the seep; the hollow), 303 (the ridge; the brow at dusk; the fold; Seln's night), 304 (the shelf at first light; the ravine's bed; the hut; the Span at noon; the watch's fire at dusk), 305 (round the fence; the shale; the blanket; one fire; the step; Karis's lamp; Seln's return). No season, month or weekday name; no figure for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
   866	
   867	**Where everyone is.** Twelve and a mule in one camp under the step, at one fire in two halves: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin; Teague, the tall man, the broad man, the young one, the older healer; Oryn and the brown mule. Seln is back from the gap and is to look again at first light; nobody moves until he has. Cleon is under Treswick. Pike is at Lowmarch. The watch's seven went east along the perimeter path on the morning of the 304th and have not been seen since.
   868	
   869	**Cael.** Nineteen. **Thirteen fragments. Deployment since the Line thirty-three** (thirty-two, and the read at the seep on the 302nd). The thirteenth (Force-adjacent, from Teague, at the timbers, at a stride) is unused; he has lined it dry once and taken his palm away; he knows that its cost would come out at the old three ribs, low on the left, and has that to tell Oryn "when she'll hear it". **Teague is not told**; the debt is entered beside the first (Vastin's). He has told Lira; Brom has it from her. The twelfth has taken two unbidden looks (the west pier's lowest course; the blanket) and been refused twice; never inward; never on a person. **The two words are still told to no one.** He stood on the Span's crown at noon on the 304th: nothing. He kept a captain's left for three breaths with a stick and opened nothing; he stood inside the line at the pinch with the eleventh asking and the thirteenth listening and told both no. He drew the shelf for Teague and asked one term of his field. He counted a course of fifty-two as fifty-one, twice (ruling *hold*). He has not put the date on any page; he has not written his own third page. He has heard Karis fix the point and say the figure (marker 10). He has not touched the cord (a hundred and thirty-seven days on the 305th) or opened the dividers. Body: a stave's bruise on the left collar-bone, ten days from the 304th; the ribs talk when the thirteenth has ground; eyes paid on the night of the 304th and to be paid for the blanket.
   870	
   871	**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. The arm is an arm. She read the herd beside Teague, walked Cael in and out under it, went a stride over the fourth line and back ("It's the same"), stood in the row of five, and did not move her feet when the broad man fell. She coaches the boy and is watched by him. She knows the thirteenth and that Teague is not told; she saw the dry stance. She does not know the two words.
   872	
   873	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. **He went grey at the shelf on the 304th and took two bolts** (breastbone; left forearm): two bruises, a week of colours, not mended. Both arms to the shoulder; he drew a leaf of shale with them at the seep and broke a rafter at the dead hold. He carries the broad man's pack on the mended shoulder. **The purse: a hundred and twenty-three.** He laid three coppers of his own on the watch's keg. His week under Oryn's eye ended on the 305th.
   874	
   875	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three; no point struck. She has: the cord's figure at the Stair confirmed; nine sheets of the piers' inner faces; one word turned on the west pier (marker 8); the lean of fourteen sheets, entered as Cael's and unchecked; the two corner signs read as an old-style year, lying among eleven years of one hundred of which the skin's year is one; the point ringed with a thumbnail; **the lamps finding**, said aloud and filed on a leaf torn from her notebook, which is now in the back of that notebook with the line "Second page: nothing entered. Not for want of a pencil."; the two slips entered as present, under two unlike seals, unnamed. She has said the figure once (marker 10). She holds one new bar numbered thirty-four with the stroke and bar. She knows that a six-word sentence exists and has not said or written it. She still has not said the office's compass point or its figure in lengths aloud. Left palm in linen; she writes; she carried a box one-handed.
   876	
   877	**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. He read three ages of iron in the fence and the watch's habits from the grass; counted seven out; looked at the gap from a mile and saw nothing, and does not like it. He has seen a keg's hoop and five made heels at the seep. He gave the watchman's stave to Cael. The case is on his breastbone, shut; nothing about it is altered; not mentioned aloud.
   878	
   879	**Vastin.** No office; no age stated. **Right knee: day twenty-six of thirty on the 305th**; Oryn's linen and two laths; stick; he walked the whole leg in the file, a stride behind Brom. He said on the 303rd that he would not stand a wall and did not. **He stood inside the fourth line on the 304th, fifth of five; the sigil went out for the first time in his life and came back "to the grain".** He has said "Noted" a third time (to Karis's two pages). He began the sentence about the apparatus and the sigils and was stopped. He read the oldest row through, found the two slips, read both aloud, knows both seals and has named neither; he drafted nothing. He made room for the broad man's stick. He does not know the mechanism, the eleventh (his own), the twelfth, the thirteenth, the two words, the date, or that the lean of the rows was seen. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it.
   880	
   881	**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, provisional. **Five days past the cairn on the 305th** (she looked up her road once at noon on the 300th and walked on east; her reasons were a shoulder's week, a knee, and an untested edge). She knit the broad man's shin on the 304th, asked first and answered in a word, and was grey for a quarter of an hour; she read it again on the 305th inside the older healer's binding. She counted Brom over the fourth line: "Four. The same." She would not spend on Brom's bruises or be told the count of fragments across the iron: **she has not been told of the thirteenth.** She has not heard the leaf; she was at the fire, not the blanket. Nobody has died under her hands. Three holds are still owed, with word sent.
   882	
   883	**Teague and his crew.** His right arm is in linen to the shoulder on a slat; the wrist and the elbow went at the timbers; he has been warned about a third time (marker 7). He said "Noted" for the first time on the 303rd. He did not turn when the broad man fell, and has told the broad man why. He thanked Cael for his left side. **He does not know that anything came to Cael at the timbers.** He knows what lies under the watch's hide and has left the reading of it to Karis. The broad man: right shin knit and bound to a board; a trestle's leg for a stick; his crossbow's stock split; he has said "Aye" to Vastin and to Oryn and nothing else to any of the six. The tall man has said nothing to any of them; he stopped the boy with a hand at the seep, kept Teague's right at the timbers, cut the stick. The young one: stepped over stake thirty-four fourth ("Four"), stood at the pinch, held when the broad man fell, ran when he might; he walked the seep at dusk. The older healer has spoken to none of the six; she set the shin and nodded once to Oryn. **Teague's four have seen:** five people stand inside the line and come out whole; a boy with a stick. **They have not been told:** the mechanism, any fragment, the leaf, the list, the lamps finding, the two slips, the date, who Vastin was, or the doctrine "behind it". No wall has been drilled or stood.
   884	
   885	**The watch.** Seven, hooded, faceless, unnamed, one with a Path that throws light. It saw: a big man take two bolts on Iron; a Force put a barricade a body's length; five people cross the iron, walk sixty strides inside it, and stand; an old man on a stick among them. **It saw nothing work inside the line, and no light, crack or named thing from either crew.** Nobody was killed or taken. It went east.
   886	
   887	**Objects and money.** **127 → 123** (the 300th: four marks at a hold's gate for two water-skins, meal, a cheese and corn). No other spending from the purse. Coppers, kept apart from it as the closed text keeps them: one for the mule's bucket on the 301st; three of Brom's own on the watch's keg. The reserve is sealed in the third box. On the mule: three boxes (the fifty-two sheets, with fourteen of them and the nine new ones handled on the 305th and put back), the flat, meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas. With Karis: the hide with its pinned sheet (the prick now ringed with a thumbnail, uninked), the Ternhall brass, her notebook (the torn lamps leaf in its back), Cleon's roll, the sheet of three boxes, Vastin's copied page, nine sheets of the piers, one new stake thirty-four. With Cael: Hesk's book, the dividers shut in it, the fair copy of the leaf (laid on the blanket folded and returned). With Vastin: the tarred kit case (cord, mallet, stake thirty-two, never driven; the cord was used at the Stair by Karis and put back). The two slips are pinned again under the knot of the oldest row's tape, in the flat. Left at the watch's post: its hut, fire, keg, meal, bolts, mallet, cord, eleven new bars, a sound crossbow on the baulk, a stave. Ten water-skins between the crews (two bought on the 300th).
   888	
   889	**Who knows what.** The mechanism: six, as before; Cleon knows how one fragment came. **The thirteenth: Cael, Lira, Brom** (Karis and Seln by Lira or the log; not staged); not Oryn, Teague or Vastin. The two words: Cael alone. The lean of the rows: Cael, Karis, Lira, Brom. The corner's year and the ringed point: the five at the blanket and Vastin; the figure itself, Karis and Cael (marker 10). The lamps finding: Karis, Cael, Lira, Brom, Vastin; nobody has laid it on the leaf, aloud or silently. The two slips: the same five; the seals' owners: Vastin alone. The date: Cael and Seln, each alone, unchanged. The short row: Cael, Karis, Lira.
   890	
   891	**Open threads.** Ten markers. A gap in the hills where seven went and nothing shows. A thing that listens and has never been let go, whose owner is forty yards off and not told. Two debts of one kind. A healer who has not been told a count, and has ribs to hear about. A sentence six words long that is in nobody's book. A third page that was kept off a blanket. Two seals that one man can name. A ring in a sheet of paper with no ink in it, two days off. A boy who goes where he is looked at. A captain with one arm. A week that ended today, and a healer who is still here.
   892	
   893	### Next-movement inheritance (Sol plan audit §8; also written into the next packet)
   894	Movement 9 must inherit the following surviving particulars in addition to its packet:
   895	
   896	- **Fragments and knowledge:** thirteen fragments; **deployment thirty-three** (coordinator ruling: the read at the seep on the 302nd stands and is counted). The thirteenth is Force-adjacent from Teague, partial Bronze, unused; it listens along a braced heel-to-palm line and costs back along that line. Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln know of it; **Oryn has NOT been told** (coordinator ruling: fix 25 declined — she refused the count at the fence on the 304th, and Cael means to tell her when she will hear it); Teague and Vastin do not. Teague is the second unpaid acquisition debt, beside Vastin. The twelfth has leaned outward at the west pier and at fourteen made sheets, never inward here. The two words *still/set* remain Cael's alone (`chapter-50.md:121–157`; `chapter-51.md:55–75,311–351`; `chapter-52.md:71–101`; `chapter-53.md:75–151`).
   897	- **What went east:** seven hooded watch members left singly with a day's start. They saw Brom take two bolts on silent Iron, Teague move the barricade with silent Force, and five people—including a boy and an old man on a stick—stand and walk inside the line. They saw nothing work inside and nobody die. They carried the broken bow; the sound bow and one stave remained at the post (`chapter-50.md:35–65,99–105,181–301`; `chapter-51.md:7–11`).
   898	- **Bodies:** the broad man's right shin is knit, boarded and stick-bearing; his crossbow stock is split. Teague's right wrist/elbow are in linen to the shoulder on a slat and the hand is unreliable; a third use would mean a splint. Brom has a breastbone bruise and ridged left-forearm bruise through a week of colours. Cael has a ten-day left collar-bone welt. Vastin's right knee is day twenty-six of thirty. Two men—Vastin and the broad man—are on sticks (`chapter-51.md:15–37,79–175`; `chapter-52.md:3–9`; `chapter-53.md:17–67,265`).
   899	- **Teague's crew:** they know five people crossed and stood whole and that a boy did it with a stick; they do not know mechanism, fragments, leaf, lamps page, slips, date, Vastin's former office, or “behind it.” The young one follows where he is looked at; the tall man and older healer still have not spoken to the six (`chapter-50.md:181–299`; `chapter-51.md:79–175`).
   900	- **Three record objects/pages:** (1) Karis holds the torn lamps-finding leaf in the back of her notebook, filed on its own; (2) Cael holds the folded fair copy of the chamber leaf in Hesk's book/coat, still not quoted; (3) the technician's sheet remains at the foot of the second row in the flat, its deep-layer date known separately to Cael and Seln and said/written by neither. No line joins (1) and (2), and Cael added no page of his own (`chapter-52.md:181–221`; `chapter-53.md:263–275`).
   901	- **Map point and notch:** the fifth point is a thumbnail ring around the prick, uninked until corded. The bearing runs through the square notch; Seln looked from a mile, saw no fire, person, movement or heel-mark, disliked the absence, and will look again from nearer at first light before Teague moves (`chapter-52.md:149–157`; `chapter-53.md:233–261,281–289`).
   902	- **Oryn:** five days past the noon-300 cairn; she stayed for Brom's week, Vastin's knee and the large edge, with three holds still owed and word already sent. She has not heard the chamber leaf. She does NOT yet know of the thirteenth or of what it would cost his ribs (coordinator ruling), and does not know *still/set* (`chapter-47.md:195–245`; `chapter-53.md:25,265`; fix 25).
   903	- **Seln:** he has looked at the pass and said only “I looked at it.” His case remains shut on his chest, contents unnamed (`chapter-49.md:187–219`; `chapter-53.md:233–261`).
   904	- **Day, bodies, money and load:** night of the 305th; twelve people and the brown mule; purse 123; no purse spend after the four marks. The mule bears three boxes, the flat, meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas. Karis has the hide/pinned sheet, brass, notebook, Cleon's roll, three-box sheet, Vastin's copied page and nine pier sheets; Cael has Hesk's book, shut dividers and folded fair copy; Vastin has the tarred kit case with cord, mallet and never-driven stake thirty-two. The two slips are re-pinned under the oldest row's knot, seals unnamed (`chapter-52.md:41–69,225–283`; `chapter-53.md:263–289`).

