   800	## AFTER MOVEMENT 8 — chapters 47–53, days 299–305 (drafted 2026-10-12, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
   801	
   802	### Coordinator rulings (binding)
   803	- **Entry seam with Movement 7 ratified** (Sol plan audit): dawn of the 299th at Millrace ford; twelve and a mule in Teague's march order; the contract's ten; purse 127; Vastin day twenty, walking; Teague's wrist in linen; twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two.
   804	- **The leg (the 299th–303rd).** The Stair's rim at noon on the 299th: Karis laid the kit's cord on the dead surveyor's figure (nine lengths and a piece, old iron to floor: "I am not checking the place; I am checking the cord"); her marker stone had been lifted and a turf relaid "since the thaw" (Seln: "Somebody has been round this place with a spade and made it agree with his sheet."). Teague began teaching Cael to read ground ("a piece of ground's a sum"; three things worth a fist: out of its place; stopped and ought to move; moving and ought to be stopped). **The cairn at noon on the 300th**, at the bend before the Hall's marsh, where a mule-path goes north over a saddle to three holds: **Oryn looked up it once and walked on east.** Her sum: Brom's shoulder wants a week of her eye (to the 305th), Vastin's knee is on her linen, and there is an edge twice any she has stood at; the three holds have had word ("a week, or more"). **Count her days past her road from this cairn** (one on the 301st … five on the 305th). She passed the chock-stones (locked Book 7's north fork) on the 302nd without a look. **Purse 123** (four marks at a hold's gate on the 300th: two skins, meal, a cheese, corn). A keeper said that a man on a bay had ridden through two days before and told him a crew would want water; two holds on the east road were barred at noon with nobody on the walk. No face, no name.
   805	- **The seep (the 302nd).** Nineteen shale-backs on the slope over the only water. Teague's reading led (never below them; never loud below them; the hour, the old cow, the way in from the west; three steps and a stand; no Path opened on that hill). The young one started down too fast and **the tall man stopped him with a hand on the breastbone, wordlessly.** **Cael asked leave and used the read on the ledge (six breaths; the eyes for an hour): a bucket of water behind a loose leaf of shale; he wanted Pressure and went without; Brom drew the leaf with both arms.** *Ruled against the audit:* the use stands. **Deployment since the Line: THIRTY-THREE from the 302nd.** A keg's hoop and five made heels at the pan: the post is watered from that fold.
   806	- **The crest (the 303rd, dusk).** The fourth place: a fence of iron bars a pace apart round a bowl; in the middle a grey arch on two piers over a sink — the carters' name, from Teague, is **the Sunken Span**. On a shelf between a dry ravine and the iron: a hut, a fire, kit under a hide, two squared timbers on trestles, **seven hoods (two crossbows, four staves, one low practitioner who shows a white light)**. Protected: "They knew." (Karis); "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one cold term." (Seln); "Drawn?" (Teague); "Nobody declares. Nobody dies. They're seven people on a posting. Noted?" (Cael) / **Teague's FIRST "Noted."** Vastin entered beforehand that he will not stand a wall (twenty-four of thirty).
   807	- **Seln (cutaway).** Three ages of iron in the fence and a path trodden a hand deep into the shale outside it: a posting far older than one cold term, kept on somebody's form. The practitioner keeps three yards from the bars: he alone of the seven has something the line would take. The case is on Seln's chest, **shut**; it "altered nothing about the case". He lay beyond the gap (a stride and a half between the last bar and the ravine's lip) to count what went out.
   808	- **THE SPAN FIGHT (the 304th, first light).** (1) The watch called "Stand where you are, and declare"; nobody answered. Brom walked the shelf with Iron Skin up, silent, and took two bolts (breastbone; left forearm). (2) Teague went up the middle at a walk with **Cael at his left a stride back**, keeping his left side with the alley's cut stave for three breaths (a stave's shoe on Cael's left collar-bone; he did not give the stride). Teague put the barricade a body's length; the recoil went to the wrist **and then the elbow**. Protected: "Through." (Teague). **THE THIRTEENTH: Force-adjacent, from Teague, acquired at a stride** — protected, Cael's own cataloguing, printed once in italics: "Force-adjacent. Teague. Partial. Bronze. Impulse along the line of the frame at contact … Deployment: none. Thirteenth." It does not ask; it **listens**. **Teague is not told.** (3) The watch reformed with one bow. Teague asked Karis whether the ground past the iron would bear a body ("It is ground."). Protected: Cael's entry before the act, "Nothing was gained inside."; "By count." (Cael). **Five went over stake thirty-four: Cael, Lira, Karis, the young one ("Four."), Vastin** ("I am forbidden a wall. I am not, I think, forbidden to stand."); four stayed on the shelf (Teague, the tall man, Brom, the broad man with the second bow). Every ordinary Path went at the stride and came back whole at the stride ("It is all there … To the grain," Vastin); a place of twice the measure does as the three did. The five walked sixty strides inside the iron to the gap and stood: **eleven seconds**. "You'll die in there." (one of the watch) / "We've been in three times." (Cael). Cael refused the eleventh at the gap and the thirteenth at the ravine's lip. (4) **At the fourth second the watch's bow shot at the broad man's; he went over the ravine's lip with a yard of rotten shale, and Teague did not turn.** The seven went east through the gap one at a time and were not followed. **Win sentence (protected):** "The crews had removed the watch's ability to hold the approach by making the only safe retreat a line the watch would not cross and the crews would." **Nobody died. Nothing was opened inside the line.**
   809	- **What the watch saw and carried east:** silent Iron taking bolts; silent Force shifting timber; five people — one a boy, one an old man on a stick — standing whole inside the line. Nothing working inside; no Path named.
   810	- **Costs.** **The broad man: the RIGHT shin (his good leg) broken clean;** laid straight by the older healer on her board and **knit by Oryn, asked first and answered in a word** (a quarter of an hour; she was grey; the two healers nodded to one another); he walks on a stick cut from the watch's trestle. **Teague's right arm: in linen to the shoulder on a slat, the hand not shutting** — protected: "A third time on that arm and I'll set it in a splint. That's not a healer's opinion. That's a fact about a line." (Oryn) / "Noted," (Teague) / "Everybody says that now," (Oryn). Brom: two bruises, "a week of colours"; he carries the broad man's pack. Cael: a welt on the left collar-bone (ten days). The young one held his ground inside the line when the broad man fell, by watching Lira's boots.
   811	- **Teague (cutaway).** "Four." He counted the young one as a man and knows now that the boy "will go wherever he is looked at, a half-beat before he has seen what is there". He kept his rule about ledges against one of his own. Under the hide: meal, bolts, a mallet, a knotted cord, and **a dozen new bars stamped with two figures and a stroke with a bar** (they stay at the post). He knows nothing of the mechanism, the fragments, the leaf or the lamps page.
   812	- **The Span itself (the 304th, noon).** Six went down (Karis, Lira, Brom, Seln, Vastin, Cael); Oryn tried Brom at the iron first ("Four … The same.") and would not be told a count across it. The arch is of the grey, in one piece with its piers, a cart's width, **no step**: a road on its back, never wheeled. **Cael stood on the crown: nothing.** The thirteenth listened to the grey; the old three ribs ached low on the left — the cost will come out of him there. Lira found the **square notch** in the hills on the line. Under the arch the sink goes down without a bottom; the piers' inner faces are cut in the floors' hand, and **Karis can read it**: nine sheets drawn. Protected: "Through" (Karis, of a word on the west pier). **Cael counted a course of fifty-two signs as fifty-one, twice** (ruling: hold). The twelfth took one unbidden breath of that course: *Goes.* **The log of the 304th (protected, whole, once):** "Twelfth—no, count it again—thirteenth … Tomorrow I find out what standing in the middle of the first one feels like." (He let "tomorrow" stand: three days by the office's figure.)
   813	- **Who knows the thirteenth:** Cael; Lira ("Thirteenth. His. A line."); Brom; Karis and Seln by the log. **NOT Teague, NOT Vastin** (two unpaid debts, entered side by side). **Oryn has not been told** as of the 305th — she refused the count at the fence; Cael means to tell her when she will hear it.
   814	- **The shale camp (the 305th).** A slow day behind two men on sticks; a halt under a step of shale four or five miles short of the notch. **One blanket:** the hide turned to the notch; one sheet of the Fallow, three of the Stair, one of the Hall and the nine of the piers, each laid as its wall stood; the flat; her notebook at the list, Cleon's roll, the sheet of three boxes; **the folded copy of the leaf under a pebble at one corner, unopened.** The twelfth, unbidden, over fourteen sheets: **every row leans the one way, along the brass, east** (entered by Karis as Cael's single unchecked glance). The fifth place's two corner signs are **a year written by its first letters in the old town's count**; Karis has one other year in that count (at the leaf's head), worked it alone that night, and will say it once, to the nearest hundred and "or near it". The point is a **thumbnail ring** round the divider's prick, uninked until corded.
   815	- **THE LAMPS FINDING** (protected, Karis's, aloud, from her table of every crossing by seven people): "They fail the way a hundred lamps fail when one wire's cut. Not the way a hundred souls fall silent." Vastin: "If a man designed the apparatus, then the sigils —" (stopped). Karis: "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." **Two pages:** she tore the ruled leaf out and laid it at the corner farthest from the folded copy, with the whole blanket between and nothing across. **Vastin's THIRD "Noted."** **Cael did not add his own third page** (the technician's sheet stays at the foot of the second row; its day unsaid, unwritten; only he and Seln have done that sum).
   816	- **The two slips**, pinned under the knot of the oldest row's tape (protected): "*Findings under the fifth column to be held. Not for onward transmission. Not for citation. Not for the seat.*" (red wax) / "*Objection entered: the holding of a finding is not the finding's disproof. Refer to the seat.*" (dark wax, a different seal). Vastin: "Somebody wanted this buried. Somebody else put it in writing that it shouldn't be. That's not a monolith. That's a crack." / "The Compact," … "Yes. Part of it." (both Vastin's). **He knows both seals and names neither**; the slips are re-pinned where they were; nobody pried.
   817	- **One fire** on the 305th (wood for one), in two halves. Vastin moved his stick a hand's breadth to make room; **the broad man: "Aye."** — his first word to the six. The healers' third exchange: the older healer held her own binding open and Oryn's hands went in under it. Teague to Cael: "You kept my left … I never had the place behind my shoulder stay so full."
   818	- **Force, dry.** Behind the step Cael set heel to a rib of rock and palm to a slab and lined himself until the thirteenth "stood"; he did not let it go; the ribs gave one clear line of warning. "A trial; not counted." Lira and Brom saw it.
   819	- **Karis (cutaway).** She knows that a six-word sentence exists and neither says nor writes it; the two pages lay a hand apart on the box lid; her entry: "*Second page: nothing entered. Not for want of a pencil.*" *Ruled against the audit:* this is the plan's refusal and is no join.
   820	- **Seln on the notch:** a square gap, water-cut, a dry bed going in, the only way through for five miles either hand; no fire, nobody on either wall, not a heel-mark, though seven went that way a day ahead. "I looked at it." He looks again from nearer at first light before Teague moves a stick.
   821	- **The close of the 305th (protected, whole):** "It's here," Karis said. "Third-tier, documented four hundred years back — as old as the record, as old as the Architect, as old as the machine. The first one they made, or near it." … "Because every other site, my Path worked while everyone's died. I want to know what the *oldest* one does to me. I think it's going to tell me something the records can't." / "He was right. He did not yet know how right." **"Four hundred years" and "the Architect" stand nowhere else in the movement.**
   822	- **State at the night of the 305th:** twelve and the mule under the shale step; **thirteen fragments; deployment thirty-three; purse 123**; Vastin **twenty-six of thirty**; Oryn five days past her cairn; Teague's arm on a slat; two men on sticks. **Names:** none minted. **Length:** about 37,200 against 35,000, accepted.
