   240	- **What went east:** seven hooded watch members left singly with a day's start. They saw Brom take two bolts on silent Iron, Teague move the barricade with silent Force, and five people—including a boy and an old man on a stick—stand and walk inside the line. They saw nothing work inside and nobody die. They carried the broken bow; the sound bow and one stave remained at the post (`chapter-50.md:35–65,99–105,181–301`; `chapter-51.md:7–11`).
   241	- **Bodies:** the broad man's right shin is knit, boarded and stick-bearing; his crossbow stock is split. Teague's right wrist/elbow are in linen to the shoulder on a slat and the hand is unreliable; a third use would mean a splint. Brom has a breastbone bruise and ridged left-forearm bruise through a week of colours. Cael has a ten-day left collar-bone welt. Vastin's right knee is day twenty-six of thirty. Two men—Vastin and the broad man—are on sticks (`chapter-51.md:15–37,79–175`; `chapter-52.md:3–9`; `chapter-53.md:17–67,265`).
   242	- **Teague's crew:** they know five people crossed and stood whole and that a boy did it with a stick; they do not know mechanism, fragments, leaf, lamps page, slips, date, Vastin's former office, or “behind it.” The young one follows where he is looked at; the tall man and older healer still have not spoken to the six (`chapter-50.md:181–299`; `chapter-51.md:79–175`).
   243	- **Three record objects/pages:** (1) Karis holds the torn lamps-finding leaf in the back of her notebook, filed on its own; (2) Cael holds the folded fair copy of the chamber leaf in Hesk's book/coat, still not quoted; (3) the technician's sheet remains at the foot of the second row in the flat, its deep-layer date known separately to Cael and Seln and said/written by neither. No line joins (1) and (2), and Cael added no page of his own (`chapter-52.md:181–221`; `chapter-53.md:263–275`).
   244	- **Map point and notch:** the fifth point is a thumbnail ring around the prick, uninked until corded. The bearing runs through the square notch; Seln looked from a mile, saw no fire, person, movement or heel-mark, disliked the absence, and will look again from nearer at first light before Teague moves (`chapter-52.md:149–157`; `chapter-53.md:233–261,281–289`).
   245	- **Oryn:** five days past the noon-300 cairn; she stayed for Brom's week, Vastin's knee and the large edge, with three holds still owed and word already sent. She has not heard the chamber leaf. She now knows thirteen and the rib cost but does not know *still/set* (`chapter-47.md:195–245`; `chapter-53.md:25,265`; fix 25).
   246	- **Seln:** he has looked at the pass and said only “I looked at it.” His case remains shut on his chest, contents unnamed (`chapter-49.md:187–219`; `chapter-53.md:233–261`).
   247	- **Day, bodies, money and load:** night of the 305th; twelve people and the brown mule; purse 123; no purse spend after the four marks. The mule bears three boxes, the flat, meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas. Karis has the hide/pinned sheet, brass, notebook, Cleon's roll, three-box sheet, Vastin's copied page and nine pier sheets; Cael has Hesk's book, shut dividers and folded fair copy; Vastin has the tarred kit case with cord, mallet and never-driven stake thirty-two. The two slips are re-pinned under the oldest row's knot, seals unnamed (`chapter-52.md:41–69,225–283`; `chapter-53.md:263–289`).
