   324	   old: `He read it over.\n\nHe had written *tomorrow*, and it was three days, by an office's figure, and a little less; he had seen the divider's point come down on a clean sheet. He looked at the word for a while, and he let it stand. It was not a true count; it was the truth about how near the thing had come, and he had no other word for that.`
