   331	21. `manuscript/chapter-52.md`
   332	   old: `"It is a year, in the count that those books keep. It is the year of the first sheet that anybody ever drew upon that place; and it was put down by a person who reckoned as the old town reckoned, before there was any office to give it a number." She sat back upon her heels. "I have exactly one other year in that count. It stands at the head of a thing that I read aloud, once."`
   333	   new: `"It is a year, in the count that those books keep. It tells me the series began before the office numbered as it does now. It does not give me a figure here."`
