17-### Bodies, injuries, people and knowledge
18-
19-- The draft advances Vastin correctly from day twenty on the 299th to day twenty-six on the 305th (`chapter-47.md:185`; `chapter-53.md:265`), keeps the right knee in linen/laths and him on a stick, and never gives him an age (`chapter-47.md:7–13`; `chapter-49.md:33–49`; `chapter-53.md:23–35`). His crossing at `chapter-50.md:205–211,315–319` does not spend the court line: Book 7's closed rule is that every ordinary Path dies inside a site, and Movement 9 may make the same fact evidentiary at the drawn stride.
20:- Teague's right wrist and then elbow take the Force recoil (`chapter-50.md:99–113`); the arm is in linen to the shoulder on a slat by `chapter-53.md:61–69`. The protected warning is missing only because marker 7 remains (`chapter-51.md:15–23`; fix 15).
21:- The broad man's right shin—the good leg—is broken, set, knit, boarded and later borne on a trestle leg (`chapter-50.md:325–367`; `chapter-52.md:3–9`; `chapter-53.md:17–57`). That follows the edition plan, although the superseded source used the bad leg (`source chapter-19.md:115–127`). The unheard consent on the 304th is to Oryn, not “to the six”; his first word to the six remains “Aye” on the 305th (`chapter-50.md:337–343`; `chapter-53.md:27–47`).
22-- Brom's two bolt bruises and “week of colours,” Cael's left collar-bone welt, Karis's bound left palm, and Oryn's quarter-hour grey are all carried (`chapter-51.md:25–37,49–53`; `chapter-53.md:51–57`). Nobody dies and there is no gore (`chapter-50.md:99–105,299–301,325–367`).
23-- Teague's four see five bodies stand and walk inside the line; they are not told the mechanism, a fragment, the leaf, the lamps finding, the slips, the date, or the doctrine “behind it” (`chapter-50.md:181–299`; `chapter-51.md:79–175`). No wall drill occurs. Teague's “place behind my shoulder” thanks at `chapter-53.md:63–67` is a personal field observation, not the pass-morning doctrine.
