4. **ch50, before the crossing:** `Nothing was gained inside.` — it is CAEL's entry, made before a boot goes over; only that sentence is fixed. Frame it as his (in his head, in the form he would write it; italics as you set his entries). If it doubles Karis's last two sentences just above ("Nothing that we do not …"), trim hers.
